// §14 entry 2 -- index computed on a folded copy, applied to the original
// -> EXS-E0332.
//
// §5.1, verbatim (this fixture is that example, wrapped in a function):
//
//   firma abassus = via.plica_unicode()
//   firma ubi     = abassus.quaere("/")?      // positio<abassus>
//   firma pars    = via.sectio(0..ubi)?       // EXS-E0332: branded to `abassus`
//
// `quaere` returns `positio<'t>`, generatively branded to the buffer it
// indexed (here, `abassus`, the case-folded COPY). `sectio` accepts only
// its own brand, so applying `ubi` to `via` -- the ORIGINAL, un-folded
// buffer -- is exactly CVE-2026-24895's class (§2.1: "case folding changes
// UTF-8 byte length, shifting a path split so SCRIPT_FILENAME points at an
// uploaded .txt"). §5.1: "This makes CVE-2026-24895's class
// unrepresentable rather than discouraged."
//
// DEFERRED, and the blockers are THREE, each independently sufficient. Named
// separately because one of them just moved and the other two did not:
//
//   1. The brand syntax this entry depends on, `positio<'t>`, is `[OPEN]` in
//      §8.6 -- no grammar exists for a lifetime-style brand parameter.
//      `EXS-E0332` itself is implemented, but unreachable through this
//      fixture's shape until the brand syntax parses
//      (`docs/design/checker.md` section 2.6).
//   2. `quaere` and `sectio` have no declaration site. `plica_unicode` now
//      does -- a `checker/types/prim.inc` prelude row keyed on the receiver's
//      type kind -- so `firma abassus = via.plica_unicode();` type-checks and
//      `abassus` is a `textus` rather than the error type. That is a real
//      move and it changes nothing here: `quaere` and `sectio` need brand
//      syntax in their own signatures, so they cannot be written down as
//      ordinary prelude rows the way the four text operations were.
//   3. `?` has no meaning the LANGUAGE defines (§8.6) and `eventus` is
//      uninhabited (`docs/design/sum-types.md` section 2), so
//      `eventus<positio<'t>>` is a type nothing can produce a value of.
//
// Measured with a fresh `exsc` from the working tree, `--diagnostica json`,
// against THIS file: `{EXS-E0305}` twice, unchanged in COUNT and changed in
// LOCATION. Before the text-method rows the two were `via.plica_unicode()`
// and `via.sectio(...)`, with `abassus.quaere(...)` silent because its
// receiver was already the error type (no cascade). Now they are
// `abassus.quaere` and `via.sectio` -- the two this entry is actually waiting
// on. Still not the `{EXS-E0332}` §14 requires.

publica functio corrige(via: textus) -> textus poscit alloc {
    firma abassus = via.plica_unicode();
    firma ubi     = abassus.quaere("/")?;
    redde via.sectio(0..ubi)?;
}

